description":"Will be fixed / added to WorldEdit, eventually","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-10-17T12:23:21Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T12:33:08Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### The Problem\n\nAccording to the docs, there is currently no `-s` flag on the `//stack` command to also stack the selection.\n\nThere is actually an undocumented effect of `-s` to `//stack`, though not what I would expect. Currently specifying ` -s` leads to a selection around the last pasted instance of the stack.\nWhat I would expect is for the selection to include the original and all pasted instances.\n\n**Use case**: Currently, stacking in two directions requires two commands _and_ adjusting the selection inbetween. This feature would make the middle step obsolete.\n```\n//stack 3 east\n[Adjust selection, could be replaced by -s]\n//stack 3 north\n```\n\n### A Solution\n\n- If current `-s` behaviour is unintentional: Change the flag to the behaviour described above.\n- If current `-s` behaviour is intentional: Add a new flag that has the behaviour described above (e.g. `-ss`, if duplicate letters are no problem, although I suspect they are).\n\nIn both cases, the flags should be added to the documentation.\n\n### Alternatives\n\n_No response_\n\n### Anything Else?\n\n_No response_","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EngineHub/WorldEdit/issues/3038/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EngineHub/WorldEdit/issues/3038/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":nu