ng the latest or recommended version of my platform software.\n- [x] I am NOT using a hybrid server, e.g. a server that combines Bukkit and Forge. Examples include Arclight, Mohist, and Cardboard.\n- [x] I am NOT using a fork of WorldEdit, such as FastAsyncWorldEdit (FAWE) or AsyncWorldEdit (AWE)\n\n### Bug Description\n\nWhen you //paste -e an block with a cushion inside of it, it doesn't paste it correctly but looks like it's placed 0.5 off on coordinates.\n\nExample:\n1. I do //cut -e or //copy -e:\n<img width=\"1467\" height=\"835\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b7c84f0a-2a94-45dc-97c7-94598a1e4fc4\" />\n\n2. I use //paste -e:\n<img width=\"1490\" height=\"796\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c636f678-ca1e-40c2-83a0-ed1266f0b4f6\" />\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nYou expect it to place the cushions exactly at the same spot as where it was.\n\n### Reproduction Steps\n\n1. Place a stairs (or any other block).\n2. Use wooden axe with the block inside the selected coordinates.\n3. //cut -e or //copy -e\n4. //paste -e anywhere.\n5. Check result.\n\n\n### Anything Else?\n\nFirst time I report a bug, so I hope I did it the right way. I also couldn't find it if someone reported it already.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EngineHub/WorldEdit/issues/3023/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":2,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EngineHub/WorldEdit/issues/3023/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EngineHub/WorldEdit/issues/3022","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EngineHub/WorldEdit","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EngineHub/WorldEdit/issues/3022/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/EngineHub/WorldEdit/issues/3022/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Engin